istances, and compare to Table 10.)>>endobj488 0 obj<</Dest(G1485475)/Next 487 0 R/Parent 465 0 R/Prev 489 0 R/Title(5. If the resistances appear to be abnormal, it will be necessary to measure the resistance at the compressor fusite terminals.)>>endobj489 0 obj<</Dest(G1485474)/Next 488 0 R/Parent 465 0 R/Prev 490 0 R/Title(4. If the resistances are correct then reconnect power leads to appropriate terminal.)>>endobj490 0 obj<</Dest(G1485473)/Next 489 0 R/Parent 465 0 R/Prev 491 0 R/Title(3. Measure the resistance to ground for each lead.)>>endobj491 0 obj<</Dest(G1485472)/Next 490 0 R/Parent 465 0 R/Prev 466 0 R/Title(2. Measure the resistance between YEL to RED, YEL to BLK, and RED to BLK and compare to Table 10 values. Each resistance set should be equal.)>>endobj492 0 obj<</Dest(G1487980)/Next 459 0 R/Parent 457 0 R/Prev 493 0 R/Title(7. Leave Users Manual with owner. Explain system operation and periodic maintenance requirements outlined in manual.)>>endobj493 0 obj<</Dest(G1750064)/Next 492 0 R/Parent 457 0 R/Prev 494 0 R/Title(6. Re-install red service port caps.)>>endobj494 0 obj<</Dest(G1487979)/Next 493 0 R/Parent 457 0 R/Prev 495 0 R/Title(5. Tighten service valve stem caps to 1/12-turn past finger tight.)>>endobj495 0 obj<</Dest(G1487978)/Next 494 0 R/Parent 457 0 R/Prev 496 0 R/Title(4. Ensure that all wiring and tubing is secure in unit before adding panels and covers. Securely fasten all panels and covers.)>>endobj496 0 obj<</Dest(G1720793)/Next 495 0 R/Parent 457 0 R/Prev 497 0 R/Title(3. Record final charge on the outdoor unit charging label with permanent and legible writing.)>>endobj497 0 obj<</Dest(G1720797)/Next 496 0 R/Parent 457 0 R/Prev 458 0 R/Title(2. Ensure all thermistors are making good contact with the tubes they are mounted to.)>>endobj498 0 obj<</Dest(G1719867)/Next 456 0 R/Parent 454 0 R/Prev 499 0 R/Title(4. Break vacuum with an inert gas purge of the refrigerant circuit ensuring that the outlet of 