nts shall be protected against mechanical damage, excessive stress by torsion, or other forces. They should be checked for mechanical damage annually.)>>endobj512 0 obj<</Dest(G1705580)/Next 511 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 513 0 R/Title(17. Certified piping and components must be used in order to protect against corrosion.)>>endobj513 0 obj<</Dest(G1705579)/Next 512 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 514 0 R/Title(16. Piping should be installed to reduce the likelihood of hydraulic shock damaging the system.)>>endobj514 0 obj<</Dest(G1705578)/Next 513 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 515 0 R/Title(15. Piping and fittings shall be protected as far as possible against adverse environmental effects. For example, the accumulation of dirt and debris.)>>endobj515 0 obj<</Dest(G1705577)/Next 514 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 516 0 R/Title(14. Provision shall be made for expansion and contraction of long runs of piping.)>>endobj516 0 obj<</Dest(G1475386)/Next 515 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 517 0 R/Title(13. Isolate hanger straps from insulation by using metal sleeves bent to conform to shape of insulation.)>>endobj517 0 obj<</Dest(G1475385)/Next 516 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 518 0 R/Title(12. When necessary, use hanger straps which are 1 in. \(25 mm\) wide and conform to shape of tubing insulation. \(See Fig. 1\))>>endobj518 0 obj<</Dest(G1475384)/Next 517 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 519 0 R/Title(11. Ensure that tubing insulation is pliable and completely surrounds vapor tube.)>>endobj519 0 obj<</Dest(G1475383)/Next 518 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 520 0 R/Title(10. Do not suspend refrigerant tubing from joists and studs with a rigid wire or strap which comes in direct contact with tubing \(see Fig. 1\).)>>endobj520 0 obj<</Dest(G1475382)/Next 519 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 521 0 R/Title(9. Avoid direct tubing contact with water pipes, duct work, floor joists, wall studs, floors, and walls.)>>endobj521 0 obj<</Dest(G1475381)/Next 520 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 522 0 R/Title(8. When passing refrigerant tubes through the wall, seal opening with RTV or other pliable silicon-based caulk \(see Fig. 1\).)>>endobj522 0 obj<</Dest(G1475380)/Next 521 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 523 0 R/Title(7. Leave some slack between structure and unit to absorb vibration.)>>endobj523 0 obj<</Dest(G1705492)/Next 522 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 524 0 R/Title(6. Run refrigerant tubes with no bends with centerline bend radius less than 2.5 times the external pipe diameter.)>>endobj524 0 obj<</Dest(G1475378)/Next 523 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 525 0 R/Title(5. Ensure that vapor and liquid tube diameters are appropriate for unit capacity \(see Table 1\).)>>endobj525 0 obj<</Dest(G1475377)/Next 524 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 526 0 R/Title(4. In noise sensitive applications \(such as bedrooms\), when a lineset is mounted to ceiling joists or floor joists, the outdoor unit must be located at least 10 ft \(3.05 m\) away. If this is not possible, create a line set configuration with enough be.\..)>>endobj526 0 obj<</Dest(G1756779)/Next 525 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 527 0 R/Title(3. Variable speed units have a wide airflow range. Consider ductwork limitations at both high and low airflows.)>>endobj527 0 obj<</Dest(G1475376)/Next 526 0 R/Parent 506 0 R/Prev 507 0 R/Title(2. Locate unit away from windows, patios, decks, etc. where unit operation sound may disturb customer.)>>endobj528 0 obj<</Count -16/Dest(G1475756)/First 634 0 R/Last 635 0 R/Next 594 0 R/Parent 505 0 R/Title(Follow these steps to properly start up the system)>>endobj529 0 obj<</Dest(G1483392)/Parent 505 0 R/Prev 584 0 R/Title(Infinity® Control, Green Communications \(COMM\) Light)>>endobj530 0 obj<</Count -8/Dest(G1710430)/First 531 0 R/Last 532 0 R/Next 505 0 R/Parent 503 0 R/Prev 533 0 R/Title(Mandatory Requirements)>>endobj531 0 obj<</Count -2/Dest(G1710431)/First 582 0 R/Last 583 0 R/Next 573 0 R/Parent 530 0 R/Title(Pressure Proof Check)>>endobj532 0 obj<</Count -3/Dest(G1475731)/First 564 0 R/Last